@page "/ai/scenarios/options-theming"
@inherits AppComponentBase

<PageOutlet Url="ai/scenarios/options-theming"
            Title="AI options and theming"
            Keywords="BitAiOptionsProvider, AI chat theming, AI chat localization, dark mode chat, Material chat, density, RTL chat"
            Description="One region of a page with its own AI options - strings, what a message shows - through BitAiOptionsProvider, and its own design system, scheme, density and direction through the bit BlazorUI theme." />

<DocsArticle Eyebrow="AI scenarios"
             Title="Options & theming"
             Lead="One region of the page with its own options, design system, scheme, density and direction - the options through BitAiOptionsProvider, everything visual through the same theme as the rest of bit BlazorUI."
             GitHubUrl="AI/Scenarios/OptionsTheming/AiOptionsThemingScenarioPage.razor">

    <Badges>
        <BitTag Size="BitSize.Small" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" Color="BitColor.SecondaryForeground" Text="Bit.BlazorUI.AI" />
        <BitTag Size="BitSize.Small" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" Color="BitColor.SecondaryForeground" Text="Scripted transport" />
    </Badges>

    <ChildContent>
        <DocSection Id="demo" Title="Live demo"
                    Description="Change the controls beside the chat: they re-skin and reconfigure only the region the chat is in.">
            <DemoExample Title="A themed, configured region" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" CodeFiles="@example1CodeFiles" Id="example1">
                <AiScenarioFrame AsideLabel="Options and theme">
                    <Aside>
                        <BitStack Gap="1rem">
                            <BitChoiceGroup Label="Design system" TItem="BitChoiceGroupOption<string>" TValue="string" @bind-Value="_designSystem">
                                <BitChoiceGroupOption Text="Fluent" Value="@("fluent")" />
                                <BitChoiceGroupOption Text="Fluent 2" Value="@("fluent2")" />
                                <BitChoiceGroupOption Text="Material" Value="@("material")" />
                                <BitChoiceGroupOption Text="Cupertino" Value="@("cupertino")" />
                            </BitChoiceGroup>

                            <BitChoiceGroup Label="Scheme" TItem="BitChoiceGroupOption<string>" TValue="string" @bind-Value="_scheme" Horizontal>
                                <BitChoiceGroupOption Text="Light" Value="@("light")" />
                                <BitChoiceGroupOption Text="Dark" Value="@("dark")" />
                            </BitChoiceGroup>

                            <BitChoiceGroup Label="Density" TItem="BitChoiceGroupOption<string>" TValue="string" @bind-Value="_density" Horizontal>
                                <BitChoiceGroupOption Text="Compact" Value="@("0.85")" />
                                <BitChoiceGroupOption Text="Default" Value="@("1")" />
                                <BitChoiceGroupOption Text="Spacious" Value="@("1.15")" />
                            </BitChoiceGroup>

                            <BitToggle Label="Right to left" @bind-Value="_rtl" />
                            <BitToggle Label="French strings" @bind-Value="_french" @bind-Value:after="RebuildOptions" />
                            <BitToggle Label="Show usage" @bind-Value="_showUsage" @bind-Value:after="RebuildOptions" />
                            <BitToggle Label="Show model name" @bind-Value="_showModelName" @bind-Value:after="RebuildOptions" />
                            <BitToggle Label="Show timestamps" @bind-Value="_showTimestamps" @bind-Value:after="RebuildOptions" />
                            <BitToggle Label="Show message actions" @bind-Value="_showMessageActions" @bind-Value:after="RebuildOptions" />
                            <BitToggle Label="Line numbers in code" @bind-Value="_showLineNumbers" @bind-Value:after="RebuildOptions" />
                        </BitStack>
                    </Aside>
                    <ChildContent>
                        @* The region: a scoped preset through bit-theme, the density multiplier the components compute their
                           sizes from, and the direction every component reads through :dir(). *@
                        <div bit-theme="@($"{_designSystem}-{_scheme}")"
                             dir="@(_rtl ? "rtl" : "ltr")"
                             style="@($"height:100%;--bit-layout-density-scale:{_density}")">
                            <BitAiOptionsProvider UiOptions="_options">
                                <BitAiChat Session="_session" Suggestions="_suggestions" />
                            </BitAiOptionsProvider>
                        </div>
                    </ChildContent>
                </AiScenarioFrame>
            </DemoExample>
        </DocSection>

        <DocSection Id="options" Title="Options">
            <p>
                <code>BitAiOptionsProvider</code> cascades a <code>BitAiUiOptions</code> to every AI component inside it, so a
                page or a region of one sets its preferences once rather than on every component: the string table
                (<code>Strings</code>, a <code>BitAiStrings</code> subclass for another language or another tone), what a
                message shows (<code>ShowUsage</code>, <code>ShowModelName</code>, <code>ShowTimestamps</code>,
                <code>ShowMessageActions</code>, <code>ShowLineNumbers</code>, ...), the render interval, the virtualization
                threshold, the image policy. It renders no element of its own, and an inner provider overrides an outer one
                for its own content.
            </p>
            <p>
                The other two places options come from: <code>ai.ConfigureUi(...)</code> sets the defaults of the whole app,
                and the <code>UiOptions</code> of one <code>BitAiChat</code> configures that chat alone.
            </p>
            <p>
                The chat opens on a six-message conversation built in code, so there is something to restyle; what you send
                goes to the transport registered for the site, which echoes it. Each option toggle (strings and the Show ones) builds a new
                <code>BitAiUiOptions</code> record (<code>BitAiUiOptions.Default with { ... }</code>): the options are
                immutable, and a new instance is what tells the provider to hand the change down.
            </p>
        </DocSection>

        <DocSection Id="theming" Title="Theming">
            <p>
                Scheme, accent, density and direction are not options of the AI components: they are styled with the global
                <code>--bit-*</code> tokens like every other component of the library, so they follow the theme there is.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>A <b>design system and scheme</b> for a region come from a scoped preset, <code>bit-theme="material-dark"</code> on any element - the Fluent&nbsp;2, Material and Cupertino presets ship with <code>Bit.BlazorUI.Extras</code>, whose bundles the host page links.</li>
                <li><b>Density</b> is the <code>--bit-layout-density-scale</code> multiplier, set in CSS as here or through <code>BitTheme.Layout.DensityScale</code> of a <code>BitThemeProvider</code>.</li>
                <li><b>Direction</b> is a <code>dir</code> on an ancestor, or the <code>Dir</code> parameter of one component.</li>
                <li>The <b>accent</b> is the site's: change it with the swatches in the header (<BitLink Href="/components/accentcolorswitcher">AccentColorSwitcher</BitLink>), and the chat follows.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Each component also has its own <code>--bit-Ai&lt;Name&gt;-*</code> variables and its <code>Classes</code> /
                <code>Styles</code> for what one component should look like differently - see its page, and
                <BitLink Href="/theming">Theming</BitLink> for the whole system.
            </p>
        </DocSection>

        <DocSection Id="components" Title="Components used">
            <ul>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/optionsprovider"><code>BitAiOptionsProvider</code></BitLink> - the options of everything inside it.</li>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/chat"><code>BitAiChat</code></BitLink> - the chat they reach, and every component it renders.</li>
            </ul>
        </DocSection>
    </ChildContent>

    <FooterTemplate>
        <DocPager Pages="AiScenarioNav.Items" AriaLabel="AI scenarios" />
    </FooterTemplate>
</DocsArticle>
